cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Autopsy: detecting vulnerabilities in AI-generated code by reasoning across dependency graphs"
abstract: >-
  Autopsy is a static-plus-LLM vulnerability detector aimed at AI-generated code.
  It builds a cross-file dependency graph, scans code in windows so that large
  files are not limited by a single pass's output budget, and includes
  deterministic detectors for deletion-based ("zero-footprint") vulnerabilities,
  where removing a comment boundary or a security control introduces a
  vulnerability that never appears as an added line in a diff. This repository is
  the reproducibility artifact accompanying the paper, including the benchmark
  harnesses and the Semgrep, Bandit, and CodeQL baselines scored by a frozen
  matcher.
type: software
